  "result": "The laundromat had a shelf labeled FREE, where people left things they couldn\u2019t quite bring themselves to throw away. There was a guide to Microsoft Excel 2003, a single roller skate, and a mug that said WORLD\u2019S OKAYEST DAD.\n\nFor three Thursdays in a row, Ana watched a man pick up the mug, turn it over, and put it back.\n\nOn the fourth Thursday, she said, \u201cNobody\u2019s going to make you prove it.\u201d\n\n\u201cOh,\u201d he said. \u201cI put it there.\u201d\n\nShe waited. Her dryer had eleven minutes left.\n\n\u201cMy daughter gave it to me when she was thirteen,\u201d he said. \u201cShe thought it was the funniest thing she\u2019d ever seen.\u201d\n\n\u201cWas it?\u201d\n\n\u201cPretty close.\u201d\n\nHe turned the mug over again. There was a little square of felt stuck to the bottom.\n\n\u201cShe put that on because I used to set it down too hard in the morning. Her room was right over the kitchen.\u201d\n\nAna folded a pillowcase. \u201cDoes it still work?\u201d\n\nHe set the mug down. Neither of them heard a thing.\n\nWhen his wash was done, he packed the mug between two towels. Ana took the Excel book. Her kitchen table had been wobbling since June.",
